242
00:14:51,946 --> 00:14:53,914
<i>You. On the ledge.</i>

243
00:14:54,081 --> 00:14:55,946
<i>This is the police.</i>

244
00:14:56,117 --> 00:14:57,675
<i>Move away from the window.</i>

245
00:14:57,852 --> 00:14:59,479
<i>Move to your right.</i>

246
00:14:59,653 --> 00:15:02,087
<i>A firefighter is there to assist you.</i>

247
00:15:02,256 --> 00:15:04,588
<i>Move to your right. Slowly.</i>

248
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:08,351
<i>- Slowly.
- Is he all right?</i>

249
00:15:08,529 --> 00:15:10,360
Yeah, they got him. He's fine.

250
00:15:10,531 --> 00:15:14,433
<i>Hello, Ms. Black. Hello, Your Honor.</i>

251
00:15:16,237 --> 00:15:18,330
<i>Have a nice night.</i>

252
00:15:23,544 --> 00:15:25,876
- You look a little crazed.
- Aren't you?

253
00:15:26,046 --> 00:15:28,276
- About what?
- People on the ledges.

254
00:15:28,449 --> 00:15:32,045
- Helicopters buzzing you.
- The price of fame, Harry.

255
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:33,448
Is it worth it?

256
00:15:33,622 --> 00:15:36,921
Dan was wrong.
I netted $8 million last year.

257
00:15:37,092 --> 00:15:39,652
- You netted $8 million?
- Craven?!

258
00:15:39,828 --> 00:15:41,921
I lost my contact lens
when I was here before.

259
00:15:42,097 --> 00:15:44,361
Craven, you get your skulking carcass
out of here.

260
00:15:44,533 --> 00:15:45,966
Isn't an introduction in order?

261
00:15:46,134 --> 00:15:49,968
- Bull.
- Oh, please. Not... No Bull. No, please.

262
00:15:50,238 --> 00:15:51,830
Yeah?

263
00:16:05,687 --> 00:16:08,155
- Male.
- Female.

264
00:16:21,237 --> 00:16:23,398
- Male.
- Female.

265
00:16:35,451 --> 00:16:38,716
So where are you planning
to take me to dinner?

266
00:16:39,255 --> 00:16:40,813
Jennifer, we have to talk.

267
00:16:41,624 --> 00:16:44,991
- You asked me, you're paying.
- Yeah, I know. Come here.

268
00:16:45,161 --> 00:16:48,028
We've got to have a serious talk.

269
00:16:48,698 --> 00:16:50,757
Okay, but I warn you.

270
00:16:50,933 --> 00:16:53,959
Daddy won't give us his blessing
after only one date.

271
00:16:54,136 --> 00:16:57,833
Jennifer. I'm afraid it's gonna be
impossible to...

272
00:17:02,278 --> 00:17:06,544
Docket update. Check it over,
and then I'll post it.

273
00:17:06,949 --> 00:17:10,442
- Miss Tuttle, I'm busy.
- Aren't we all.

274
00:17:11,121 --> 00:17:15,023
I'll look at this when I have a chance,
and if I have any comments, you'll know.

275
00:17:15,425 --> 00:17:16,949
Fine.

276
00:17:18,395 --> 00:17:21,831
I caught you at the Garden. Nice show.

277
00:17:23,867 --> 00:17:27,826
Come on. We're not gonna get
any peace around here.

278
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:42,443
The coast is clear.
Jennifer, you okay in there?

279
00:17:42,619 --> 00:17:46,282
Fine, thanks. I've done this before.

280
00:17:46,456 --> 00:17:48,356
We'll meet you there, Your Honor.

281
00:18:02,106 --> 00:18:05,371
- Hey, mama.
- Hey, kiss off.

282
00:18:11,049 --> 00:18:13,415
- Hi.
- Hi.

283
00:18:15,753 --> 00:18:20,122
I can fit all my toiletries in one handbag.

284
00:18:23,628 --> 00:18:25,528
Sign here.

285
00:18:32,637 --> 00:18:35,936
- Female.
- I agree. No bet.

286
00:18:38,843 --> 00:18:43,212
You know, it was all so simple
in the '40s.

287
00:18:50,789 --> 00:18:52,450
All clear.

288
00:18:57,096 --> 00:18:58,927
Very nice.

289
00:18:59,098 --> 00:19:03,728
Well, I never thought I was gonna
say this to anyone, but...

290
00:19:04,670 --> 00:19:06,069
...would you care to join me?

291
00:19:06,238 --> 00:19:08,206
I'd be delighted.

292
00:19:08,374 --> 00:19:09,602
Have fun, you two.

293
00:19:09,775 --> 00:19:12,437
I knew you were gonna say that.

294
00:19:17,783 --> 00:19:19,250
So.

295
00:19:19,418 --> 00:19:23,787
What's a nice girl like you
doing in a place like this?

296
00:19:24,490 --> 00:19:28,051
All right, autographs with pens, $ 10.

297
00:19:28,827 --> 00:19:31,955
Personalized stationery, used tissue,
that sort of thing...

298
00:19:32,131 --> 00:19:34,361
...strictly supply and demand.

299
00:19:36,835 --> 00:19:38,996
Do I have an opening bid?

300
00:19:40,807 --> 00:19:42,035
So...

301
00:19:42,208 --> 00:19:45,268
...we didn't sneak off to the men's room
to hold hands, did we?

302
00:19:46,212 --> 00:19:47,907
Jennifer.

303
00:19:48,248 --> 00:19:51,684
- I like you a lot.
- I like you a lot.

304
00:19:51,851 --> 00:19:53,648
But it's not that simple.

305
00:19:56,189 --> 00:19:58,316
You're married, and you didn't tell me.

306
00:19:58,491 --> 00:20:00,516
Something like that.

307
00:20:01,327 --> 00:20:04,490
- I'm not married to another woman.
- Well, you don't mean...

308
00:20:04,664 --> 00:20:07,656
No, no. What I mean is...

309
00:20:07,834 --> 00:20:10,098
...I am married to an idea.

310
00:20:10,270 --> 00:20:14,070
The idea of becoming the best judge
that I can be.

311
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:17,767
But with all your fans, and the hoopla,
the press, the attention...

312
00:20:17,944 --> 00:20:19,377
You're dumping me, aren't you?

313
00:20:20,647 --> 00:20:23,707
- You're not mine to dump.
- I could be.

314
00:20:25,785 --> 00:20:27,377
Jennifer.

315
00:20:28,154 --> 00:20:33,286
You are the sweetest person
I have met in a long, long time.

316
00:20:33,461 --> 00:20:36,589
You can call it intuition,
you can call it a gut feeling...

317
00:20:36,764 --> 00:20:40,666
...but I knew that from the first moment
I laid eyes on you.

318
00:20:40,835 --> 00:20:43,065
And what makes it even
more magical is that...

319
00:20:43,237 --> 00:20:45,364
...it was just a chance meeting.

320
00:20:45,539 --> 00:20:49,635
Because if I had set out
to look for someone...

321
00:20:49,810 --> 00:20:53,473
...it would have been someone
just like you.

322
00:20:55,716 --> 00:20:59,083
We want to be alone.

323
00:21:04,925 --> 00:21:09,624
- Well, I guess that's that, huh?
- Jennifer, I'd like to see you again.

324
00:21:09,797 --> 00:21:12,095
- But...
- But it's hard right now.

325
00:21:12,266 --> 00:21:15,724
I can't serve justice with all this
happening around me, it's not possible.

326
00:21:15,903 --> 00:21:19,430
I know. Same thing happened
with a man I met in Los Angeles.

327
00:21:19,607 --> 00:21:20,939
He owned a crystal shop.

328
00:21:22,310 --> 00:21:25,074
Twelve thousand in damages the first week.

329
00:21:25,914 --> 00:21:28,007
- Jennifer.
- Being on the road so much...

330
00:21:28,183 --> 00:21:31,744
...it's hard to know anyone
long enough...

331
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:35,686
...to find out if there's even a possibility
for a long-term relationship.

332
00:21:36,258 --> 00:21:39,318
Sounds to me like you want
a long-term relationship.

333
00:21:39,928 --> 00:21:42,021
So sue me. I'm a romantic.

334
00:21:42,697 --> 00:21:44,790
Then you have some choices to make,
don't you?

335
00:21:46,268 --> 00:21:49,169
Yeah. I guess I do.

336
00:21:51,106 --> 00:21:53,700
- You know that feeling I told you about?
- The gut one?

337
00:21:53,875 --> 00:21:55,638
Yeah. I got another one.

338
00:21:55,811 --> 00:21:58,006
I know that somewhere, sometime...

339
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:00,410
...we are gonna see each other again.

340
00:22:01,416 --> 00:22:03,145
I feel it too.

341
00:22:03,318 --> 00:22:05,013
- But.
- But?

342
00:22:05,187 --> 00:22:11,593
Next time, we meet in the ladies' lounge.
It's a better class of graffiti.

343
00:22:17,533 --> 00:22:20,434
Sign where I've indicated.

